      "level": 2,
      "content": "FUNDAMENTAL RIGHTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Right to Equality spans Articles 14–18, ensuring equal protection and non-discrimination.",
        "Right to Freedom encompasses Articles 19–22, protecting core democratic liberties.",
        "Right against Exploitation (Articles 23–24) prohibits human trafficking and child labor.",
        "Right to Freedom of Religion (Articles 25–28) guarantees freedom of conscience and religious management.",
        "Cultural and Educational Rights (Articles 29–30) safeguard minority interests.",
        "Right to Constitutional Remedies (Article 32) empowers citizens to move the Supreme Court for enforcement of rights."
      ],
      "id": "z0s1n4n"
    },
